&lt;p class=&quot;MsoListParagraph&quot; style=&quot;margin-left:18.0pt;mso-add-space:auto;
text-indent:-18.0pt;mso-list:l0 level1 lfo1&quot;&gt;&lt;b&gt;Car Parking&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family:&amp;quot;Aptos&amp;quot;,sans-serif;mso-ascii-theme-font:minor-latin;
mso-fareast-font-family:Aptos;mso-fareast-theme-font:minor-latin;mso-hansi-theme-font:
minor-latin;mso-bidi-font-family:&amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-bidi;
mso-fareast-language:EN-US&quot;&gt;Notwithstanding&amp;nbsp;the details submitted with the
application, prior to first occupation of the development, a Car Parking Design
and Management Plan shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the Local
Planning Authority. This shall include details of how parking will be allocated
and details of any measures to discourage private motorised vehicle use such as
charging regimes. Parking shall be made available for staff only and residents
shall not be eligible to use the car park. The agreed measures in the Car
Parking Design and Management Plan shall be implemented upon first occupation
and maintained thereafter in perpetuity.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

